&+W======================================================================&n
&+Y                           DURIS PLAYER NEWS&n
&+W======================================================================&n
&+WUpdated: October 17, 2026&n

Welcome back! Catch up on September 15 to October 17, 2026 below.
The newest changes come first; later updates replace older rules.
Earlier coverage, back to December 14, 2025, and the archive follow.

&+R10/17/26&n &+L-&n &+YPets should not bar the door&n
&+W----------------------------------------------------------------------&n

&+Y-&n A saved pet with more health, mana or vitality than its current maximum
  no longer prevents you from logging in. Its resources settle to the
  restored maximum when it returns.
&+Y-&n Pets with invalid saved vital stats are held for staff review while
  you enter the game. Their saved equipment is retained.

&+R10/16/26&n &+L-&n &+YNews at a glance, errands back on the road&n
&+W----------------------------------------------------------------------&n

&+Y-&n Your prompt now shows &+Y(news)&n when you have unread player news.
  Turn paging on with &+C'toggle page on'&n and open &+C'news'&n to clear it.
  Each character remembers which update you opened across logins;
  a later update brings the reminder back. Refreshed news also stays
  consistent when the game restarts.

&+CEpic errands have destinations again&n
&+Y-&n The restored roster gives epic tasks &+Y107&n eligible zones to choose
  from. Already-completed zones remain excluded for your character;
  this does not reset your history, epics or existing task.
&+Y-&n New characters can receive earned epic tasks during their first
  session. A task waiting for its destination can be assigned once its
  zone choices and your history are ready, without earning it again.
&+Y-&n A failed refresh keeps the last usable list of task zones. Restarting
  during a refresh no longer leaves you with only part of that list.

&+CTravel that follows your instructions&n
&+Y-&n Teleport, Depart and Etheric Gust can now work in limited-teleport
  zones when the destination is within the allowed five-room range.
  Other travel restrictions still apply.
&+Y-&n If you have Plane Shift, &+C'innate plane shift Air'&n now passes your
  chosen plane correctly. A missing or invalid plane name no longer
  spends that innate's use. Gate staves also keep your typed destination.
&+Y-&n Full innate names choose the power you asked for: &+C'innate summon warg'&n
  no longer selects Summon Horde when you have both powers.

&+CTraps still bite, but looting knows when to stop&n
&+Y-&n Bulk looting stops if a trap kills, moves, puts you to sleep or
  immobilizes you, or takes away the container you were looting.
  Rejected pickups no longer continue with success messages or follow-up
  actions. These cases also avoid crashes from handling vanished targets.
&+Y-&n Spent trap charges on items in player corpses now stay spent after
  a restart. Saved carried items and pets' items also retain trap state.
  This preserves newly saved state; it cannot recover old missing records.

&+CCharacter saves, titles and the high seas&n
&+Y-&n Base attributes above the old small-number limit can now save without
  wrapping or rejecting the save. Staff stat edits write the complete
  value and reject numbers that do not fit; gameplay stat caps still apply.
&+Y-&n After a failed final save, logging in again can load your last saved
  state once the old session's save attempts finish. This does not recover
  changes that never saved.
&+Y-&n Guild titles longer than &+Y512 bytes&n, including colors and the guild
  name, are rejected before they can break your character save.
&+Y-&n Sinking or removing an NPC ship no longer stalls ship activity or
  leaves other ships following a vanished escort or boarding target.
&+Y-&n The &+MTotem of Mastery&n and &+MCirclet of Light&n now name the item properly
  in their whisper activation messages.

&+R10/15/26&n &+L-&n &+YFamiliar roads and clearer rules&n
&+W----------------------------------------------------------------------&n

&+CThree routes worth another look&n
&+Y-&n &+MOutcasts Tower&n is back on the Good Continent, south of Kimordril.
  Follow the scorched trail north from the Hearth Valley grasslands.
  Its old entrance now leads through ordinary DarkPeak foothills.
&+Y-&n &+MArcium&n now lies northwest of Evermeet on the Good Continent.
  Enter west from the foothills or north from the Myrabolus valley.
  Its former jungle approaches now lead into the surrounding hills.
&+Y-&n A stone stair connects the &+MChasm of the Misty Vale&n to the
  &+MUnderdark&n. Descend from the misty cliff trail, or climb back up
  from the narrow tunnel below; the passage works in both directions.

&+CFair play, clear expectations&n
&+Y-&n Read &+C'help rules'&n for the consolidated rules. Conflicting older
  copies have been removed; &+C'help immortals'&n reflects the staff policy.
  Staff may not actively play player characters; active players may not
  serve as staff. This applies across all of a person's accounts and
  characters: stop playing before joining staff, or step down to play.
&+Y-&n Reporting a bug does not permit continued exploitation. Report bugs
  with &+C'bug'&n and keep exploit details off public channels and boards.
  Use &+C'petition'&n to ask staff about uncertain behavior or report abuse.
&+Y-&n The rules explicitly cover harassment, threats, private information,
  impersonation, account access, spam, false reports and punishment
  evasion. PvP and corpse looting remain part of Duris; they do not excuse
  misconduct. Keep disagreements civil and respect other players' privacy.
&+Y-&n Unattended play and letting another player control your character
  through triggers are prohibited. Check &+C'help robots'&n for client-action
  limits and &+C'help multi-playing'&n for the limited inn-storage exception.
  That exception does not allow alt assistance in combat, scouting,
  travel or corpse retrieval. Ask staff before using uncertain automation.

&+R10/15/26&n &+L-&n &+YThe winds have changed their treasures&n
&+W----------------------------------------------------------------------&n

&+Y-&n Hunting wind artifacts? &+MYan-C-Bin&n now carries the &+Mdagger of Wind&n,
  while &+MAkadi&n carries the &+Msphere of wind&n. Their rewards have traded places.
&+Y-&n The dagger's wind escape no longer triggers for monsters wielding it.
&+Y-&n To unleash the sphere's whirlwind, wear it and &+C'rub sphere'&n.
  Rubbing another item no longer sets it off. The whirlwind respects safe
  rooms and avoids friendly targets; its &+Y500-second&n reuse time remains.
&+Y-&n Reavers using &+MThrym's Icerazor&n now receive its intended extra cold
  damage while Coldshield is active. Slow no longer grants that bonus.

&+CYour client keeps up with you&n
&+Y-&n Supported client panels fill in your status, effects, group, room,
  quest and combat target when you log in, reconnect or re-enable them.
  Purchased quest maps return too, including while you are morphed.
&+Y-&n Group panels update when members leave and when their health changes,
  even if those members do not use panels. The displayed group limit now
  follows your side's actual limit. Combat panels track starts, ends and
  damage more accurately.
&+Y-&n Ship panels refresh when you step onto a bridge and clear when you
  leave it. Room and item names no longer show stray escape backslashes.

&+CReaching staff and planning your training&n
&+Y-&n The optional staff-only Discord petition feed now shows your actual
  character name, even when hidden or invisible. Staff replies identify
  both characters there too. In-game visibility rules stay the same.
  This replaces the earlier news about concealed names showing as Someone.
&+Y-&n &+C'help epic skill cost'&n lists first-step and full-training prices,
  including the extra cost when only your secondary class can learn a skill.
  Ask your teacher for the exact cost of your next lesson.
&+Y-&n Website hints and &+C'credits'&n have refreshed links and information.
&+Y-&n MUD listing services can now read Duris's live player count and uptime.
  This count includes connected mortals in the game, not staff.

&+R10/14/26&n &+L-&n &+YBattle records and your website presence&n
&+W----------------------------------------------------------------------&n

&+Y-&n New PvP battle records again retain each participant's level, class,
  name, guild, race, equipment and public combat log as they were captured
  before death. Long public logs now fit; older missing text is not restored.
&+Y-&n New characters start with Web Info enabled. Use &+C'toggle webinfo off'&n
  if you do not want the extra character details shown on the website.
  Existing characters keep their saved setting.

&+R10/14/26&n &+L-&n &+YPetitions can reach the Gods on Discord&n
&+W----------------------------------------------------------------------&n

&+Y-&n An optional staff-only Discord feed can now carry your accepted
  &+C'petition'&n messages and staff replies, even with no Gods online.
  Concealed names appear as Someone, and dollar signs stay as typed.
  Delivery is best effort; Discord messages cannot reply into the game.
  Your usual in-game petition controls and delivery still work as before.
&+Y-&n Scheduled reboot warnings now show the reason supplied by staff.

&+R10/14/26&n &+L-&n &+YEpic adventures at every level&n
&+W----------------------------------------------------------------------&n

&+Y-&n You can earn epic points at &+Yany level&n, including from enemy kills,
  runestones and epic potions. The old level-50 earning requirement is gone.
  Epic skill lessons still begin at &+Ylevel 30&n, with their usual costs and
  other requirements.
&+Y-&n &+C'score'&n shows your total earned epics and current task at every level.
  If the Gods assign you a task, you can check it again after reconnecting.
&+Y-&n An epic potion stays in your hand or pack if its award cannot be given.
  A successful quaff consumes one potion and awards &+Y75 epic points&n.

&+CRewards, training and recovery&n
&+Y-&n Artifact and guild rewards now keep up correctly when you earn several
  epic awards in quick succession, including across saves and reconnects.
&+Y-&n Epic boons report whether points were actually awarded. Paid epic
  training updates derived hit points and client displays immediately,
  and announces when you master the skill.
&+Y-&n Healing correctly clears an incapacitated or stunned posture once
  you recover. Combat stops processing a strike when either fighter dies.
&+Y-&n Area listings stay within their output limit and show corrected zone
  averages. Help now covers &+C'web spray'&n, &+C'seadog'&n and &+C'quickstep'&n.

&+CHometown warnings and racial shrug&n
&+Y-&n Evil hometown invasion alarms are enabled, using the same alarm
  chances and timing as before. Good hometown alarms remain enabled.
&+Y-&n Grey Elf shrug returns to &+Y30&n and Drow Elf shrug to &+Y38&n.

&+R10/12/26 - 10/13/26&n &+L-&n &+YOld battle rhythms and earlier epic training&n
&+W----------------------------------------------------------------------&n

&+CFive allies, one chance to open the next level&n
&+Y-&n A qualifying kill now needs a base share of at least &+Y0.20 frag&n:
  no more than &+Yfive&n of the killer's side may be in the room, including
  the killer and ungrouped allies. Level-based frag bonuses cannot make
  a larger force qualify. The timer, leading-side and victim-level
  requirements still apply; &+C'fraglist'&n shows the current requirements.
&+Y-&n Kills made before this update cannot unlock a level under the new rule.
  Your existing frags and unlocked levels remain yours.

&+CEpic lessons from level 30&n
&+Y-&n You can begin learning epic skills at &+Ylevel 30&n, down from level 56,
  if you meet the skill's other requirements and can pay its epic-point
  and platinum costs. Use &+C'epic skills'&n to find the available teachers.
  Earning new epic points still requires &+Ylevel 50&n; stone costs are unchanged.

&+CYour race's familiar rhythm returns&n
&+Y-&n Melee attacks become faster for Drow Elves, Grey Elves, Halflings,
  Gnomes, Tieflings, Goblins, Driders and Kobolds.
&+Y-&n Melee attacks become slower for Barbarians, Mountain Dwarves, Duergar
  Dwarves, Ogres, Trolls, Thri-Kreen, Centaurs, Minotaurs and Firbolgs.
  These restore the older racial melee rates. Racial spellcasting rates,
  attributes and innate powers keep their current settings.
&+Y-&n Newly created copies of affected equipment regain their old combat
  and spell speed bonuses, replacing the attributes previously given
  in exchange. &+WEquipment you already saved keeps its saved bonuses.&n
&+Y-&n A spirit totem summoned at &+Ylevel 56&n or above once again improves
  casting speed instead of granting the replacement &+Y3 Wisdom&n.

&+CEarthen fists, recovery and connecting&n
&+Y-&n Greater Earthen Grasp gives victims a better chance to resist
  paralysis: the caster's Strength advantage has a smaller, capped
  influence on the save. Ordinary Earthen Grasp, including the Earth
  Reaver version, keeps its existing saves. Hold durations are unchanged.
&+Y-&n Positive character regeneration returns to its normal baseline,
  removing the reduced recovery setting.
&+Y-&n Browser connections handle delayed connection details correctly,
  so login limits count your own address instead of confusing players
  sharing the website's connection to the game.
&+Y-&n &+C'help boon'&n now explains current boon requirements and rewards,
  participation toggling, and how to spend boon shop stat points.

&+R10/12/26&n &+L-&n &+YNew roads, sharper blades and a blood bargain&n
&+W----------------------------------------------------------------------&n

&+CYour next level is your side's next victory&n
&+Y-&n Good and Evil now unlock one level at a time. Once the timer expires,
  the side leading in total frags needs a fresh qualifying frag to unlock
  its next level. On equal totals, either side can claim the next unlock.
&+Y-&n Levels between spell circles open for the winning side. Circle levels
  &+Y31, 36, 41, 46, 51 and 56&n open for everyone. Other sides use that shared
  cap. Each unlock starts a &+Ythree-day&n wait; an expired timer alone does
  not grant a level. The old cap-unlock experience boon is gone.
&+Y-&n The victim must be no more than &+Yfive levels&n below the shared cap, and
  at least one individual gain must reach &+Y0.10 frag&n. Small shares from
  several groupmates do not add together to meet that minimum. Check
  &+C'fraglist'&n for both sides' caps and the timer. Hardcore keeps its
  &+Ytwo-level&n allowance, with &+Y56&n still the maximum. Existing caps carry
  over; future new seasons begin with level &+Y30&n open to everyone.

&+CAnti-paladins: let the enemy pay your group&n
&+Y-&n Dark Knights and Demonic Riders gain the &+Y10th-circle&n spell
  &+C'blood tithe'&n. Cast it on yourself: enemy damage builds malice that
  boosts your player groupmates' weapon and spell damage in the same room.
  The caster receives no bonus. &+C'score'&n shows the available group bonus.
&+Y-&n At full charge, up to three groupmates gain &+Y12%&n damage. Larger groups
  share a smaller benefit: about &+Y9%&n with five, &+Y7%&n with eight and &+Y5%&n with
  fifteen. The bonus is halved against players. Only the strongest tithe
  applies; tithe casters and allies under Battle Lust gain no tithe bonus.
&+Y-&n Each hit feeds at most &+Y5%&n of your maximum hit points into malice, which
  loses &+Yone quarter&n each combat round. Sustaining full charge takes about
  &+Y15%&n of your maximum hit points in enemy damage per round. Your group,
  its pets and players of your own side cannot feed it. The spell lasts
  &+Y15 ticks&n plus one per ten points of Devotion.

&+CFreedom of Movement: lasting footing, later training&n
&+Y-&n Freedom of Movement moves to &+Y11th circle, level 51&n for Druids,
  Blighters, Clerics, Bards, Reavers and Rangers. Previously prepared
  copies no longer bypass your current spell-circle eligibility.
&+Y-&n While the spell lasts, takedown chances are multiplied by &+Y0.80&n and
  backstab chances by &+Y0.70&n. Takedowns no longer consume the spell for an
  outright block. Its protections against bindings and webbing still can
  exhaust it. Land travel costs &+Yone move&n per room; water costs half the
  usual movement, with a minimum of one.

&+CSwashbucklers and a better-aimed sweep&n
&+Y-&n Swashbucklers' attacks are harder to parry. Triple Attack arrives at
  &+Ylevel 41&n with a &+Y90%&n training cap, and Vicious Attack's cap rises to
  &+Y100%&n at level 56. Dual Wield remains at level 30.
&+Y-&n Legsweep now works against a foe one size category smaller or larger,
  at &+Y75%&n of the normal chance. A bigger size gap still topples the sweeper.

&+CA flight map you earn by exploring&n
&+Y-&n Use &+C'list'&n at each of &+Y25 ordinary flight carriers&n to learn its stop
  and earn discovery experience once per character. &+C'flights'&n shows your
  discoveries anywhere, even in the air. Save and relog retain them; a
  new season resets them. Alts discover their own routes.
&+Y-&n Carriers list learned destinations in distance order. &+C'buy <number>'&n
  buys the matching ticket; &+C'give ticket <carrier>'&n boards that same
  waiting carrier. Ordinary fares are &+Yhalf a platinum per room flown&n,
  with no minimum or maximum, level limit or race restriction. You must
  see the carrier. Passing a ticket to an alt does not teach the stop;
  old route tickets may need replacing.
&+Y-&n Discovery rewards grow with your discoveries: your current EXP-gain
  cap times the number of stops learned, divided by &+Y27&n, before normal
  racial, rested and difficulty adjustments and limits. You still learn
  a stop when unable to gain EXP; no repeat reward is saved for later.
&+Y-&n Extra Destinations remain separate one-way journeys: Storm Port's
  Stronghold costs &+Y10 platinum&n; the Snow Ogres cavern approach costs
  &+Y50 platinum&n; the Desolate Island approach to Scorched costs &+Y200&n.
  Both epic trips require &+Ylevel 51&n. Their departure dragons and entrances
  are outside the ordinary network, with no passenger return service.

&+CShifting home and sailing for profit&n
&+Y-&n Githyanki, Illithid and Pillithid prime shifting now includes Clavikord,
  Bugentolen, Storm Port and Quietus Quay in place of Killing Fields,
  Drustl, Crescent Chasm and Kelek. Each picks an eligible room in that
  area, avoiding private, protected, hometown, ocean and groundless rooms.
  &+C'innate shift_prime'&n requires the Astral Plane, no combat and no PvP
  adrenaline. Missing destinations now fail cleanly.
&+Y-&n Deramuth cargo and contraband prices now follow measured sailing
  distances in both directions. Recheck your trade routes: &+Ycargo already
  aboard sells at the new prices&n, too.
&+Y-&n Racial innate help now lists active abilities, unlock levels and
  command names more accurately, including Web Spray and shade movement.

&+R10/11/26&n &+L-&n &+YHooves, webs and a few convincing doubles&n
&+W----------------------------------------------------------------------&n

&+CNew tricks for old races&n
&+Y-&n Centaurs gain a more useful &+C'stampede'&n at &+Ylevel 21&n. Both that command and
  &+C'innate stampede'&n work during combat and can knock down and stun enemies
  already fighting someone else. They do not force those enemies to target
  you; a stunned foe whose fight breaks resumes when its opponent hits it.
&+Y-&n Stampede is player-only, with a &+Y60-second&n cooldown. You need footing, the
  front rank and a room wider than single file. Failing those requirements
  spends no cooldown. Enemies in a group's back rank always dodge.
&+Y-&n Driders at &+Ylevel 31&n can use &+C'innate web_spray <target>'&n. A hit leaves
  &+Y30 seconds&n of undispellable webbing that drains movement each combat
  round: &+Y3 moves&n at level 31, rising to &+Y7&n at level 56. Another hit refreshes
  the web instead of stacking it.
&+Y-&n Web Spray has a &+Y5-minute&n cooldown and &+Yone combat round&n of recovery. Level
  and agility affect your hit chance; Freedom of Movement and Evade can stop
  it. A valid attempt starts combat even if it misses or is defended. Each
  completed room move gives the victim a &+Y10%&n escape chance, including
  movement while mounted.
&+Y-&n Gnomes and Kobolds at &+Ylevel 31&n can use &+C'innate reflection'&n on themselves.
  It creates one image at level 31, two at 36, three at 41 and four from 46,
  drawing attackers onto a double. It has a &+Y5-minute&n cooldown and
  &+Yone combat round&n of recovery. An existing summoned titan blocks it without
  spending either.

&+CNames and commands&n
&+Y-&n A command argument with an unfinished quote no longer repeats its own text
  while being interpreted.
&+Y-&n &+CReveal True Name&n handles random weapons with unfamiliar spell effects
  without risking a crash.

&+CYour racial strengths have shifted&n
&+Y-&n These are &+Yracial stat multipliers&n, not flat points added to your score.
  The new values replace the old ones below; race help has been updated too.
&+Y-&n Mountain Dwarves: dexterity &+Y95% to 100%&n, agility &+Y85% to 95%&n. Duergar:
  dexterity &+Y90% to 100%&n, agility &+Y90% to 95%&n, constitution &+Y135% to 125%&n,
  intelligence &+Y75% to 85%&n and wisdom &+Y130% to 125%&n.
&+Y-&n Trolls: agility &+Y100% to 90%&n, intelligence &+Y75% to 70%&n and wisdom
  &+Y90% to 95%&n. Trolls also lose their racial &+RGroundfighting&n innate.
&+Y-&n Centaurs: wisdom &+Y100% to 110%&n. Tieflings: strength &+Y110% to 100%&n and luck
  &+Y110% to 95%&n.
&+Y-&n Driders: strength &+Y95% to 120%&n, constitution &+Y115% to 120%&n, power &+Y85% to 90%&n
  and intelligence &+Y100% to 110%&n.

&+CSpell preparation: mind the race you choose&n
&+Y-&n The racial part of spell preparation has been retuned. Lower percentages
  mean faster preparation; your spell, class and other modifiers still
  matter. The new racial factors are:
&+Y-&n Gnome and Kobold &+Y70%&n; Halfling and Goblin &+Y73%&n; Drow and Grey Elf &+Y82%&n;
  Mountain Dwarf, Duergar, Githyanki and Githzerai &+Y85%&n; Tiefling &+Y87.5%&n.
  These races prepare spells faster than before.
&+Y-&n Centaur and Drider &+Y109%&n; Minotaur &+Y115%&n; Barbarian and Troll &+Y122%&n; Ogre and
  Firbolg &+Y131%&n. These races prepare spells more slowly than before. Human,
  Orc and Thri-kreen remain at &+Y100%&n.
&+Y-&n Several monster races have their stronger spell resistance restored:
  Illithids, monster Vampires, Demons, Devils, Dragons, Beholders and
  Shadows. &+WPlayable Vampires keep their existing resistance.&n The &+CRrakkma&n
  group bonus now follows its configured resistance increase correctly.

&+R10/05/26 - 10/10/26&n &+L-&n &+YClearer conversations, steadier footing&n
&+W----------------------------------------------------------------------&n

&+CKingdoms take a rest&n
&+Y-&n &+WKingdoms are disabled in the shipped configuration.&n Kingdom commands,
  upkeep and resource harvesting are inactive while that switch is off, and
  ordinary guildhall placement is available again. The September kingdom
  workshop and store announcements below describe the earlier rules, not a
  service enabled by default now.

&+CYour conversations and your privacy&n
&+Y-&n Tells, whispers, asks, says, emotes, projects, beeps, guild and alliance
  chat, jchat and shouts are no longer saved as chat transcripts by the
  game. Their message text is also withheld from the command debug log.
  &+WPetitions, nchat and staff commands remain logged.&n See &+C'help channels'&n for
  who hears each channel.
&+Y-&n Ordinary staff snooping now tells you when it starts and ends, and records
  those actions.
  &+WLevel-62 staff retain an audited silent-snoop option requiring a reason.&n
  Staff can no longer read another player's recall history. Your own
  &+C'recall'&n and the Channel spell's shared sight are unchanged.
&+Y-&n Stored network addresses now age out after &+Y30 days&n since their last use,
  with cleanup running hourly. Temporary address-lookup files are removed
  when connections close. Addresses on the ban list remain while the ban
  does.

&+CWatch that first step&n
&+Y-&n Once you are falling, movement and most commands are refused until you
  land. You see each downward tumble, so a queued walk cannot quietly turn a
  canyon fall into a landing at the inn. A teleport onto solid ground ends
  the old fall; a teleport into open air starts a new one there.
&+Y-&n Short falls hurt less: the flat part of impact damage now grows with the
  fall's speed. Long falls, the minimum damage and Safe Fall retain their
  rules. Faang's canyon-wall rooms no longer admit wandering monsters,
  though the spiders still roam the surrounding area.
&+Y-&n Broken downward loops no longer leave you falling forever. The northern
  wilderness chasm now leads to its bottom, and the Pocket of Exile lands
  you on its disc of force.

&+CQuests, boards and familiar faces&n
&+Y-&n Artifacts and outposts created during boot now keep their stored records,
  and artifact lists fill correctly after the world has finished loading.
&+Y-&n Zone-story achievements now put quest givers in their actual areas. This
  reunites progress that had split into nameless "This area" rows and
  corrects the count of fully completed zones. &+C'achievements zones'&n lists
  areas where you have completions, most completed first, with ties sorted
  by name.
&+Y-&n &+C'achievements zone <area>'&n now accepts area names properly, including
  multiword names. World-quest reward messages show the XP you actually
  receive, rather than an amount that ignores your modifiers or limits.
&+Y-&n Your bartender-quest allowance waits for your history to load before
  appearing in &+C'score'&n or your client's quest panel. The panel then updates
  automatically, instead of staying blank or displaying -1.
&+Y-&n The Black Pearl's pirates, quest characters and special items have their
  missing behavior restored, including Long John Silver's companions and the
  dragonslayer. Charing's quest givers, city services and Royal Stables work
  again, as do the City of Brass's Staff of Blue Flames and Ring of
  Elemental Control.
&+Y-&n Charing and the City of Brass now enforce their intended guild, temple and
  palace entrances: guards that had been standing idle once again check who
  may pass. The relocated CBL hall's inner sanctum also works as an inn
  again.
&+Y-&n Boards now answer only where they stand. Empty or aborted posts cannot
  borrow another board's text after a restart, and blank headlines no longer
  exhaust the shared message supply. Long headlines are safely limited to
  &+Y70 characters&n. A failed board save preserves its previous file; a damaged
  board no longer stops the whole game from starting.

&+CGear, clients and everyday play&n
&+Y-&n New CHAOS Centaurs receive their horse-body kit piece, and Driders receive
  their spider-body piece. Those slots were being checked before their
  level-one racial abilities existed.
&+Y-&n Firbolgs, Tieflings, Wood Elves, Kuo-toa and Pillithids are no longer
  mistaken for other races by equipment restrictions. They can use gear with
  a deny list that does not name them, but do not qualify for gear
  restricted to a list of other races.
&+Y-&n Large shop listings now arrive complete, including with paging off. An
  invalid item in stock no longer hides all the items after it.
&+Y-&n Relogging after an item handover and a crash no longer revives an older
  copy in the giver's inventory. Pending paid deliveries also keep the
  ownership information they need to reach you.
&+Y-&n A damaged character save is refused as damaged instead of being mistaken
  for an empty character.
&+Y-&n When your pet kills something that drops random equipment, &+Wyou&n receive the
  salvage notice. The roll still uses the pet's level and luck.
  &+C'help random equipment'&n now recognizes that full phrase.
&+Y-&n Busy moments no longer add every delayed casting segment onto the next
  one. Casts aim for their intended completion time, although a busy server
  can still delay the final segment.
&+Y-&n Monster regeneration and spell expiration are spread through the tick to
  reduce recurring pauses. Monster affects still count down once per tick,
  but may end at a different point within it. Player timers, including
  shapechanged players, keep their normal tick timing.
&+Y-&n An address may hold up to &+Y8&n connections that have not logged in; an IPv6
  /64 shares that allowance. Login prompts close after &+Y2 minutes&n without
  input, except an emailed reset-code wait, which keeps &+Y15 minutes&n. Reaching
  the connection limit does not ban you.
&+Y-&n Website logins behind the trusted proxy no longer close unrelated players'
  login windows. Active website login messages refresh the idle timer, so
  taking time to sign in does not disconnect you while you are still typing
  requests.
&+Y-&n Connection handling now avoids a server crash on a banned connection and
  releases the resources of refused secure connections.
&+Y-&n &+C'time'&n reports the server's actual timezone. Shutdown notices appear once,
  with their colors rendered, and the farewell now closes Duris like a book
  of starlight.
&+Y-&n Finishing or abandoning a text edit no longer wastes memory with every use
  or risks a crash when closing an edit.
&+Y-&n Kick messages now match insect, aquatic and beholder victims correctly.
&+Y-&n The welcome, credits and staff list now identify this Duris port. The
  rules point you to Discord or &+C'petition'&n for staff help with bugs;
  multiplaying and robots remain prohibited.
&+Y-&n The project hub and Power Atlas now point to the maintained Duris site.
  Find the main website at &+Chttps://duris.sbs/&n and the documentation and
  atlas at &+Chttps://luminarimud.github.io/Duris/&n. The project site's
  navigation also fits narrow phone screens.

&+R09/28/26 - 10/04/26&n &+L-&n &+YYour belongings, your boat, your next adventure&n
&+W----------------------------------------------------------------------&n

&+CSaving without the long wait&n
&+Y-&n Ordinary item moves, crafting, coins, epic points and frags now change in
  play immediately, with saves following afterward. Death, corpse raising
  and resurrection no longer wait on the old recovery holds. Quit, rent and
  camp return you to the account menu without waiting for the save to
  finish.
&+Y-&n &+C'empty'&n checks item restrictions before moving anything, but a container
  that runs out of room can receive only part of the load. The rest stays in
  the source. The older promise of an all-or-nothing transfer no longer
  applies to a capacity limit.
&+Y-&n Ordinary charmed creatures can receive gear again under the usual give
  restrictions. Crafted or forged items still cannot be given to monsters.
  The September restriction on giving saved gear to ordinary charmies has
  gone.
&+Y-&n &+WAn abrupt crash can lose recent unsaved progress.&n Use &+C'save'&n when you want
  a checkpoint: "Save complete" now means the save has actually been
  written. A clean shutdown saves what it can within its time limit; a
  copyover that cannot finish its saves is called off.
&+Y-&n The old death-restitution system has been removed, including its
  deleted-character recovery bags and locker notices. That September
  announcement is historical. Full-world recovery is also &+Woff by default&n;
  saved characters, pets, corpses, lockers, banks and shops do not depend on
  it. Ordinary ground loot is not a substitute for storage.
&+Y-&n Item transfers and destruction now leave fewer stale copies behind: an
  item destroyed after an older save stays destroyed. Spellbooks keep every
  recorded spell instead of only the last entry.
&+Y-&n Carrying an item with a very long world description no longer prevents
  your whole character from saving.
&+Y-&n The idle-connection timeout that could leave all later saves and loads
  waiting forever has been fixed. Account screens, listings and other stored
  information are also read without holding up everyone's commands; a
  requested list may take a moment to arrive.

&+CLockers, corpses and raised companions&n
&+Y-&n Shopkeepers keep the right stock with the right shop through saves and
  recovery, including shops that share a keeper type. Quest and tradeskill
  shopkeepers now save their stock too.
&+Y-&n A save while you are inside a locker now saves its contents too and
  remembers the room outside its door for your next login. Leaving during an
  earlier save no longer replaces newer locker contents with an older
  version.
&+Y-&n Items added to a player corpse with &+C'put'&n, &+C'put all'&n or &+C'empty'&n are now
  saved with that corpse, so the additions survive a restart.
&+Y-&n Raised undead, golems, titans, avatars and dracoliches now carry the items
  from their corpse again instead of handing the gear to the caster. Your
  owned pet's save includes that gear. Hidden monster-only pieces remain
  unequippable, even when ordered by keyword.
&+Y-&n Corpses containing older coin piles can be raised again, and raising a
  corpse no longer leaves a second saved corpse behind. Saving an offline
  character for staff or artifact maintenance no longer erases pets that
  were not loaded for that task.
&+Y-&n &+WCoins in your purse now go into your corpse when you die.&n Picking up a
  pile too large for your purse leaves the pile intact, and retrying a bank
  deposit or withdrawal no longer applies it twice.

&+CAuctions, rewards and progress&n
&+Y-&n Removing an auction now returns the winning bidder's money through
  &+C'auction pickup'&n. Bids and listing fees are reserved when you submit them
  and returned if the request fails. A buy-now bid returns any excess over
  the price.
&+Y-&n To raise your own bid, have the &+Yfull new bid&n available while the bid is
  processed; only the increase is ultimately charged. An item you list
  leaves your inventory while the listing is processed and comes back if the
  listing is refused.
&+Y-&n Your selected epic bonus now returns on login and copyover. You no longer
  need to choose it again or restart its timer to make it work; while it is
  being read, the display says it is loading.
&+Y-&n Earning epics while wearing an artifact now feeds the artifact and credits
  guild prestige correctly. Artifact lists reflect the new feeding timers.
  When an offline owner's artifact expires, their other belongings stay with
  them instead of dropping onto the floor.
&+Y-&n Spending a boon-shop stat point on a stat already at &+Y100&n now returns the
  point. Boon extensions and reactivations announce their result, and author
  filters in &+C'boon list'&n handle names containing apostrophes.
&+Y-&n Daily world-quest and shop/quest trophy counts now agree on the &+YUTC day&n,
  preventing an extra reset at local midnight. Poll creation, voting and
  expiry also use the correct times again.
&+Y-&n Very large item values no longer wrap around to a zero price, including
  the Dark Sun's cargo hold.
&+Y-&n Map updates no longer risk a crash because another character has quit or
  rented and is sitting at the account menu.
&+Y-&n Quest tag changes, achievement checks, missing polls and artifact repairs
  have guards against missing data that could crash the game.
&+Y-&n Jewels supplied in a CHAOS pouch can be used for encrusting again.
  &+CEmbrace Death&n once more adjusts its bonus as your wounds change and
  removes that bonus when you heal.
&+Y-&n Areas that do not reset on the normal schedule now use their own
  repopulation chance, rather than another area's setting.

&+CNames and accounts stay together&n
&+Y-&n A character rename now carries your account listing, ship ownership,
  personal locker, locker permissions, guild roster and leaderboard credit
  with it. Old broken account listings are repaired on login. Your old
  corpse still belongs to you for resurrection and your map marker, even
  though its name does not change.
&+Y-&n You cannot delete a character who is still in the game. A refused deletion
  keeps guilds and ships intact, and a newly created character cannot
  inherit a deleted character's identity or possessions. Characters can also
  be deleted when zone-story tracking is disabled and they have no stored
  story progress.
&+Y-&n After a copyover, quitting returns you to the correct account even when
  its name differs from your character's. Racewar side-change waiting times
  survive relogging, and character-creation locks apply to both native and
  website creation.

&+CCaptains: altitude finally counts&n
&+Y-&n Flying ships now sit &+Y4 squares&n above the water for weapon range. A surface
  ship three squares away is five squares from a flying ship; surface
  weapons with reach &+Y4 or less&n cannot hit it. Two flying ships remain level
  with one another.
&+Y-&n &+CShip Damage Control&n now reduces hull and sail hits while the owner is
  aboard. Warship sails also take &+Y15% less damage&n before that skill's
  reduction, with at least one point of damage still getting through.
&+Y-&n &+C'look sight'&n and firing messages show the actual hit percentage from the
  ship combat roll. The displayed odds changed, not the hit roll itself.
  Counter-ram damage now uses the defending ship's own ram and hull.
&+Y-&n Speed now affects your chance of crashing into the coast, so slow down
  before docking. Disembarking checks your actual position on the ship
  instead of sometimes rejecting an edge room as the middle.
&+Y-&n A ship sunk by a fleet now loses the &+Wfull frag penalty&n. The victorious
  ships still divide the reward among themselves.

&+CTrade, ownership and a berth to come home to&n
&+Y-&n Contraband bought repeatedly at the same port stacks with that port's
  contraband already aboard. Captains at &+Y1000 alignment&n can no longer buy
  it. A shipwright's summons quote now matches the amount charged, rather
  than quoting twice the price.
&+Y-&n Cargo-market swings are bounded to &+Y90% to 115%&n of their neutral modifier;
  contraband uses &+Y85% to 130%&n. These limits apply to the market's price
  adjustment, not to the entire value of a cargo load.
&+Y-&n The game saves the ship you own even when you are aboard someone else's.
  Restarts load all stored ships rather than stopping at the first hundred,
  and old summons are cleared when a ship returns.
&+Y-&n A full ship-room pool no longer silently loses a stored ship. Placement
  retries when space opens, and hull changes check for room before charging
  you or refund the cost if the room disappears during the purchase. Failed
  saves no longer turn an existing vessel into a second new ship.
&+Y-&n Boarding pirates now appear inside the ship they attacked, rather than
  another vessel's rooms. Client ship panels show the people actually
  aboard, the proper maximum sails for the hull and readable status text.
&+Y-&n Ship help now gives the actual firing arcs: &+Y80 degrees&n fore and aft,
  &+Y100 degrees&n on each side. Ships turn faster at speed; maneuvering into a
  berth requires speed &+Y20 or below&n. Use &+C'repair weapon <slot number>'&n for a
  weapon or &+C'repair all'&n for everything. Help for ship NPCs, weapons and
  &+C'toggle shipmap'&n is now available.

