  &+Wno-rent&n. Dust mephits now appear with the earth pillars, and lead dao
  guardians receive their earthen bracers.

&+CSmall repairs with a long reach&n
&+Y-&n Negative-weight items no longer subtract from your carrying burden.
  Putting them in bags, equipping them or reloading them follows the same
  rule, so nested containers cannot leave your encumbrance inconsistent.
&+Y-&n Revoking a divine-claim container now preserves its contents. Fixed
  shopkeepers no longer multiply after recovery, and the local herb dealers
  avoid a repeating interaction that could crash the game.
&+Y-&n &+CFrost Beam&n no longer forces an extra combat engagement before dealing its
  damage. This removes the unwanted opening behavior; it does not make an
  attack harmless.
&+Y-&n Broken keys stay broken after saving, and item descriptions survive
  copyover.
&+Y-&n The login banner identifies enabled STAGING, CHAOS, ALL-RACES and
  ALL-CLASSES modes. Names reserved for gods are refused during character
  creation and renaming, including website entry paths.

&+R09/15/26 - 09/21/26&n &+L-&n &+YA few more things worth knowing&n
&+W----------------------------------------------------------------------&n

&+CRecovery, books and rewards&n
&+Y-&n Positive natural hit-point, mana and movement recovery for players is now
  &+Ytwice the neutral rate&n on the shipped settings. Existing posture, race and
  spell effects still shape the amount you recover.
&+Y-&n Missing group or combat-list members and lost links during command
  confirmations no longer trigger the corresponding crashes.
&+Y-&n Restoring your position during copyover no longer spills coins as though
  you had walked there.
&+Y-&n Liches who lose a level on death now keep the proper proportion of their
  remaining XP, instead of an arithmetic mistake reducing it to a single
  point.
&+Y-&n Scribing recognizes a scroll as its source before work begins. It consumes
  or updates the scroll properly and stops if that source disappears before
  the scribing finishes.
&+Y-&n Paying a world-quest giver and immediately asking for your map now follows
  the right order. A failed or no-longer-valid map request returns its
  payment; rereading a map you have already bought is free.
&+Y-&n Encrusted and enhanced items now draw generated names from their intended
  name set, instead of switching naming styles at random.
&+Y-&n &+C'divineclaim list'&n now presents rewards, expiry, remaining copies and
  current holders in a clearer table.
&+Y-&n Staff can choose the effects in a community spell-up and repeat it at
  intervals from &+Y10 seconds to 1 hour&n, for connected players up to level 60
  on either side or both. Regeneration can be added. These are staff-run
  sessions; the repeat ends at reboot or copyover.
&+Y-&n Terminal choice 3 is now labeled for its &+CMSP presentation markup&n. Use
  &+C'toggle terminal [ansi|gen|msp]'&n to select a mode. MSP here supports
  presentation such as prompts, maps and group displays; it does not send
  sound or music triggers.

&+R09/15/26 - 09/21/26&n &+L-&n &+YKingdom works, quest records, practice targets & more!&n
&+W----------------------------------------------------------------------&n

&+CKingdom workshops and made-to-measure gear&n
&+Y-&n Kingdom leaders can expand a main guildhall with a &+Rforge&n, &+Mloom&n,
  &+Cjeweller&n and &+Yguild store&n. Use
  &+C'kingdom build <forge|loom|jeweller|store> <direction>'&n.
&+Y-&n Each room costs &+Y20,000 platinum&n from the guild treasury. A hall may
  have &+Yone&n of each, and a store needs at least one workshop first.
&+Y-&n The forge makes weapons and metal armour, the loom makes cloth and
  leather pieces, and the jeweller makes rings, bracelets and necklaces.
&+Y-&n In the store, &+C'list'&n shows the pieces your workshops can make and
  &+C'buy <item> [variant]'&n orders one. Only full members may shop, and the
  realm must be active, out of arrears and able to supply every material.
&+Y-&n Every piece is fitted to its buyer's level, up to &+Ylevel 56&n. Prices,
  weapon dice, armour and stats scale with that level; a level-&+Y56&n
  longsword, for example, costs &+Y87 platinum&n, &+Y34 mineral&n and
  &+Y14 wood&n on the shipped settings.
&+Y-&n Store gear has solid re-equipping stats but no procs or magical effect
  flags. It may be carried, dropped, looted and sold, but &+Wonly the
  original buyer may wear it&n.
&+Y-&n Alliance tribute owed now survives guild saves instead of silently
  resetting.

&+CZone-story achievements, rankings and practice targets&n
&+Y-&n Eligible static zone, story and lore quest completions are now recorded
  for each character and survive logout and restart. Repeating the same
  quest does not inflate your distinct completion total.
&+Y-&n Mortal group members in the same room when an eligible quest is completed
  receive their own completion credit too.
&+Y-&n Use &+C'achievements zones'&n for your private area summary and
  &+C'achievements zone <area>'&n for a progress bar and the
  &+Y25%&n, &+Y50%&n, &+Y75%&n and &+G100%&n milestones in one area.
&+Y-&n Use &+C'leaderboard quests [page]'&n to compare worldwide totals. It shows
  each eligible mortal's exact unique count and percentage to
  &+Ytwo decimal places&n; public standings may be up to &+Y12 hours&n behind.
&+Y-&n A profiled &+Ctraining dummy&n now waits in every distinct character-
  creation room. It stays at full health, never retaliates and records all
  damage that lands, so attacks and single-target spells can be tested safely.
&+Y-&n Type &+C'dummy report'&n to see its level, race, class, armour, saves and
  accumulated damage. Type &+C'dummy reset'&n to clear the meter for a fresh
  test.

&+CMagic, meditation and class fixes&n
&+Y-&n Meditation now continues while you use passive commands such as
  &+C'look'&n, &+C'exits'&n, &+C'inventory'&n, &+C'equipment'&n, &+C'score'&n,
  &+C'weather'&n, &+C'who'&n, &+C'read'&n and display-only &+C'group'&n.
  Coin-only &+C'put'&n commands also leave the trance intact.
&+Y-&n &+C'tupor'&n now uses the normal spell-slot recovery path, begins with your
  highest incomplete circle and gives clear feedback if it is already active.
  Waking or changing posture cancels it without the old &+Y2-second&n shock;
  hostile disruption still imposes a brief recovery.
&+Y-&n Rejected &+CElemental Aura&n casts now explain whether another aura or the
  room's terrain is the problem, and fail before consuming mana or a prepared
  spell.
&+Y-&n &+CWind Blade&n is now delivered before the game tries to wield it. If your
  weapon slot changes while it forms, the blade remains safely in inventory.
&+Y-&n Dragoon conjured weapons apply their &+Y10%&n life cost only after the weapon
  arrives. Summoned Books and Totems keep the old copy unless the replacement
  is successfully delivered.
&+Y-&n &+RDread Blade&n victims no longer keep its temporary &+Y+15 spell save&n
  after the dark spell resolves, and vampiric hit points above maximum now
  decay gradually instead of snapping straight back to maximum.
&+Y-&n Paladin aura status now clears when its last linked aura breaks.
  &+C'Unspecialize'&n also stops immediately when you have no specialization,
  so it cannot spend &+Y10 epic points&n when there is nothing to remove.

&+CItems, shops, companions and recovery&n
&+Y-&n Owned raised followers can now accept ordinary durable equipment and give
  it back safely, including backpacks with all their contents. Their carried
  and worn gear stays with them through saves, reconnects and restarts.
  Ordinary charmed creatures still refuse these durable transfers.
&+Y-&n Produced shop items can be bought in batches of &+Y1 to 50&n with
  &+C'buy <item> <container> [amount]'&n. Each item is paid for and delivered
  in order, with clear totals if only part of a batch can be completed.
&+Y-&n Commands that depend on an item now wait for an earlier item movement to
  finish. Rapid sequences such as &+C'get pick bag'&n followed by
  &+C'repair pick'&n no longer fail because the item is still arriving.
&+Y-&n &+C'Empty'&n now moves a container's complete nested contents through the
  durable transfer path, keeping the source intact if the move cannot finish.
&+Y-&n Weapons lost to a combat fumble, Fumble Gauntlets or a floor-dropping
  critical disarm now reach the room only after ownership follows them. If
  that move is refused, the weapon remains safely in your inventory.
&+Y-&n Corpse coin looting can finish after a successful &+C'flee'&n when the exact
  corpse and chosen pile remain in the original room. A full inventory now
  produces &+Yone&n carry-limit warning per bulk haul instead of one per item.
&+Y-&n Saved ground items, including nested containers, now survive repeated
  server restarts instead of disappearing after the first recovery boot.
&+Y-&n If approved recovery belongs to a character that has since been deleted,
  the belongings can be delivered to the surviving account's locker in a
  bag named for that character. A login banner points the account to it.

&+CWorld services, ships and travel&n
