&+R09/07/26 - 09/14/26 - Kingdoms, magic tune-ups, lag-free play & more!&n
&+W----------------------------------------------------------------------&n

&+CKingdoms, guards and gathering bags&n
- Missed an upkeep cycle? Don't panic: land in arrears now only loses a
  single outer square per missed cycle instead of entire rings collapsing.
- Re-school your kingdom guards for 1,000 prestige using the command
  'kingdom respec <#> <class>', or re-swear your Champion for 5,000 prestige
  using 'kingdom champion respec <class> <class>'.
- Kingdom Champions can now master specialized callings: Dreadlord, Reaver,
  Avenger, Dragoon, Blighter, Ethermancer, Illusionist, Theurgist, Summoner,
  Conjurer, or Psionicist!
- Garrison guards now come properly equipped with weapons suited to their
  class and boast healthy, reliable hit point pools everywhere.
- Unguilded gatherers rejoice! Four new Gathering Bags are now stocked in
  guildhall shops. Anyone can carry one and use 'harvest' at resource nodes
  to collect physical materials into their bag.
- Your society overview ('soc') now displays your kingdom's rings, garrison
  size and level cap, champion status, and weekly upkeep at a glance.

&+CSpells, healing and casting&n
- Healing magic plays much nicer together! Regeneration and Accelerated
  Healing now comfortably coexist without blocking each other.
- Recasting Regeneration refreshes its duration smoothly instead of locking
  you out.
- The Crown of Aramus grants its slumber regeneration independently without
  wiping away your active healing spells when you wake up.
- Type ahead while casting! Commands entered while preparing a spell now
  queue up safely instead of getting lost.
- If you need to stop casting, typing 'abort' halts your cast immediately
  without interfering with anyone else.
- If a spell gets canceled or interrupted, your casting state and mana roll
  back cleanly.
- Casters can now study and cast from their owned spellbooks even in pitch
  black darkness.
- Scribed spells inside spellbooks now safely survive storing and retrieving
  them from lockers.

&+CScore, coins and looting&n
- Track your stash at a glance: the 'score' command now displays the total
  platinum, gold, silver, and copper tucked inside any open or transparent
  containers you carry or wear!
- Picking up coins is prettier and cleaner: coin messages use shiny color
  formatting and hide empty zero amounts (e.g. "You get 5 platinum and 10
  gold" instead of a wall of 0s).
- Coins no longer count against your inventory item limit when looting, and
  messages for grabbing piles of items are cleanly spaced.
- Fixed picking up coins placed in rooms by zone builders.

&+CQuests, world and exploration&n
- Bartenders have fresh bounties! Tavern quests dynamically select safe,
  level-appropriate targets and will find fresh targets if previous ones
  were already completed.
- Ocean travel feels right: movement costs for swimming and sailing across
  water sectors are properly balanced.
- Overland and zone automaps now track your position marker ('*') accurately
  even near the far edges of a zone.
- Four-armed warriors (like Thri-Kreen) keep their preferred combat weapons
  and shields in the right hands when equipping gear.
- Fixed duplicate shopkeepers and ensured store inventories restock cleanly.

&+CCombat, death and companions&n
- Loyal companions survive reboots! Owned pets are safely preserved across
  game restarts and copyovers.
- Respawning after death cleanly restores your standing position and vitals,
  preventing ghost limbo states.
- Corpse identity and generated loot are safely tracked across server
  recoveries.
- Fixed an issue where monsters on Chaos servers had 1 hit point, restored
  proper spell scaling for leveling monsters, and gave monster area spells
  a 20% punch for thrilling group battles!
- Fixed 'grouped' accidentally toggling AFK or guild golem status.

&+CAccounts, login and ease of life&n
- Forgot your password? You can now type '?' at the password prompt to get
  a secure reset code emailed to your registered address.
- Jump right into the game! Character creation skips the old rules pop-up
  (the rules are always available via 'rules' or 'help rules').
- Browse help at your own pace! The waiting cooldown between reading help
  and info topics (like 'faq', 'rules', 'wizlist', and 'credits') is gone,
  and pages load instantly.
- Deleting an account character now gives clear, confirmed feedback.
- Rock out to Duris: check out the new Land of Bloodlust theme tracks and
  lyrics in the game records!

&+CSmoother play and lag fixes&n
- Silky smooth gameplay: account logins and password hashing now run in the
  background, eliminating the annoying combat freezes when players log in.
- Walking through crowded cities and monster lairs is noticeably smoother
  thanks to optimized room movement checks.

&+R09/06/26 - Latest fixes&n
&+W----------------------------------------------------------------------&n

&+CCoins, bags and looting&n
- Fixed cases where picking up or dropping coins could leave the wrong
  amount in your purse, on the ground, or inside a bag.
- Fixed coin handling when a character dies, including deaths that happen
  while a money command is still finishing.
- Fixed cases where a death could get stuck while moving your belongings
  to a corpse. The game now keeps the recovery information needed to
  finish the death without quietly throwing away your belongings.
- Pickup and money messages now finish before the next command prompt.
  This removes the confusing extra prompt in the middle of a pickup.

&+CCombat and ships&n
- Fixed a monster's area spells sometimes skipping the person fighting
  it when the monster aimed at someone else. This includes Death Field.
- Corrected who sees ship weapon damage messages during sea battles.


&+R09/01/26 - 09/05/26 - Kingdoms, event gear and everyday fixes&n
&+W----------------------------------------------------------------------&n

&+CKingdoms and gathering&n
- Guilds can build a kingdom around their main guildhall and expand their
  land on the world map. Start with 'kingdom help' or 'help kingdoms'.
- Use 'kingdom prospect' to check whether a location can hold a kingdom,
  and 'kingdom map' to see your land and the next square you can claim.
- Find gathering spots around the world and use 'kingdom survey' and
  'kingdom harvest'. You do not need to belong to a guild to gather.
- Claiming land costs platinum and all four kingdom resources. The cost
  grows as your kingdom expands, so larger realms take a group effort.
- Kingdom upkeep is weekly. Keep the guild treasury funded: unpaid
  upkeep blocks expansion and can eventually cost your kingdom land.
- Leaders can hire guards, promote them and raise a kingdom champion.
  'Kingdom roster' shows your guards and their promotion costs.
- Added more gathering spots on the Surface and in the Underdark.
- Fixed land placement, resource costs, guard rosters and gathering spots
  that could appear where nobody could use them.

&+CChaos events and new characters&n
- When Chaos starter gifts are enabled, new characters receive equipment
  chosen for their class, including the tools and books they need.
- Chaos events can provide starting coins, epic skills and other bonuses
  so new characters can join the action sooner.
- New Chaos characters can receive a craft pouch with a reusable supply
  of materials. Normal skill, tool and recipe requirements still apply.
  Read 'help chaos craft pouch' for the pouch's uses and limits.
- Fixed missing material names in craft pouches after a restart.
- Summoner character creation is available again.
- Gaining several levels at once produces a shorter set of messages.

&+CItems, accounts and controls&n
- Commands entered after moving items or money now wait their turn
  instead of getting lost or using an out-of-date inventory or balance.
- Fixed 'get all' failing on ordinary items dropped by monsters.
- Fixed bulk bag storage counts and saving items placed inside bags.
- Account-bound divine rewards now recognize the owning account when
  picking up or using its reward items.
- Fixed personal locker access for the rightful owner.
- Fixed the 'No Locate' toggle and its help text.
- Added permanent account deletion with confirmation and checks for
  belongings or other ties that must be dealt with first.
- Fixed several logout and connection problems, including unexpected
  disconnections for players using the website.

&+CShips and the world&n
- Fixed several problems with ship movement, automatic sailing, cargo,
  purchases and combat. Empty cargo spaces now stay correctly cleared.
- Fixed monsters that could stop following their hunting trail.
- Corrected the central terrain in Planar Prisons and broken text in
  Newhaven.


&+R08/01/26 - 08/31/26 - Smoother play and safer belongings&n
&+W----------------------------------------------------------------------&n

&+CCasting, combat and character choices&n
- Type 'abort' to stop a spell or mental power you are preparing.
  Canceling leaves a brief recovery delay. Read 'help abort' for details.
- Fixed commands being lost when canceling a spell.
- Fixed Dragoon communion order and checks for needing a mount when
  learning spells through assimilation.
- Fixed Taint doing almost no damage to many targets.
- Reduced Doombringer's special attack frequency and the number of hits
  in each burst.
- Fixed Moonwell Moonstone targeting and repeated spell fade messages.
- Druids resume their communion correctly after logging back in.
- Added help for every player race, improved the race selection screen,
  and gave new characters more time to finish character creation.
- Starting towns were corrected so their guards do not attack a new
  character simply for being a race allowed to start there.
- Stat rolling is much more consistent, with all stats in the very good
  range instead of requiring long stretches of bad rolls.

&+CSaving, deaths and valuables&n
- Improved saving of characters, equipment, pets, ships and ground items
  to reduce lost progress and duplicate belongings after interruptions.
- Fixed several problems with corpse contents, resurrection and deaths
  while disconnected. Death no longer removes a character from its
  account's character list.
- Fixed cases where one damaged saved item could stop a character from
  entering the game.
- Improved protection for bank balances, auction payments and refunds,
  epic points, guild funds and earned rewards when a save is delayed.
- Fixed bulk 'get all', 'drop all' and 'put all' commands getting stuck.
- Fixed crashes involving 'wear all', relic pickups and monsters picking
  up coins.
- Fixed ground artifacts and other items appearing twice after recovery,
  and restored equipment missing from recovered monsters.
- Corpses are no longer accepted as salvage materials.
- The 'save' command now reports when your save has finished.

&+CCrafting and equipment&n
- Encrust stones are easier to tell apart, and several less useful stones
  were improved. Encrusted items receive more distinctive names.
- Items that are both encrusted and enhanced have clearer descriptions.
- Crafted equipment no longer gets an extra random change to its stats.
- Learning encrust no longer requires craft, but its learning cost rose.
- Reciting a scroll now correctly passes along the target you named.
- Fixed travel and tracking costs for several terrain types.

&+CMaps, displays and convenience&n
- Use 'mapglyphs' to customize the symbols and colors on your world map.
  Roads connect more clearly, and distorted maps were corrected.
- Improved color display and support for different game clients.
- Login greetings appear sooner, and news is shown at account login.
- New characters start with a 40-line screen length for easier reading.
- Fixed prompts and pages appearing in the wrong order, empty-container
  feedback, and quest messages for characters already at maximum level.
- Tracking no longer lists your own tracks.
- Typing 'shipyard list' without more words shows the available hulls.
- Corrected ship naming checks and reduced delays in viewing contacts.
- The old 'who' toggle was replaced by a login-announcement preference;
  the terminal toggle works again.
- Fixed the eastern entrance of Marigot and door keywords in Cora's
  library. Winterhaven's drakenhorse was strengthened and can see
  invisible travelers.
- Fixed pets bypassing restrictions on Vecna's pillar portals.
- The old siege system was retired. The new kingdom system is described
  in the September news above.
- Reduced several causes of game pauses, delayed actions and crashes.


&+R07/01/26 - 07/31/26 - Crafting, rewards and storage&n
&+W----------------------------------------------------------------------&n

&+CCrafting, enhancement and salvage&n
- Recipe books are easier to browse and explain the materials and other
  requirements for a recipe. Unavailable recipes are filtered out.
- Crafting and forging give clearer success, failure and reward messages.
- Enhancement explains its requirements and results more clearly.
- Superior stat enhancement can improve all eligible stats together,
  with limits based on the item's original stats.
- Improved the colored marker for superior equipment.
- Examining salvageable items gives more helpful guidance. Salvage tools
  and magical essence requirements are explained more clearly.
- Fixed recipes and enhancement choices that could never produce a
  valid result, along with several crafting and forging failures.

&+CRewards and level limits&n
- Added 'divineclaim' for rewards granted to your account. Rewards can
  allow more than one claim when staff have set them up that way.
- Level-cap progress now checks an already-earned milestone when its
  waiting period ends, without needing another player kill to notice it.
- Hardcore characters can have an allowance above the normal level cap,
  while still respecting the game's maximum level.

&+CBags, lockers and auctions&n
- Fixed taking everything from corpses and bags, including bags with
  other bags inside them. Carrying and container limits are checked.
- Fixed locker contents, private chest bag order, and lockers incorrectly
  staying marked as in use after their user had left.
- Fixed auction offer times and auctions showing the wrong time left.
- The account character list updates your saved location more reliably.

&+CCombat and travel&n
- Equipment that grants sneaking works again after a successful flee.
- Typing commands while waiting now clears idle status properly.
- Fixed special attacks on shadow monsters and missing individual hit
  messages from Death Field.
- Fixed town raid timers and ordinary blocked passages failing to open
  the way back.
- Drinking a potion in a no-magic room still wastes it, but no longer
  starts the potion waiting timer.
- Identify gives correct information for scrolls, potions, wands and
  staves instead of displaying meaningless spell values.
- The Ashrumite inn accepts rent, and trying to fully repair a ship
  without enough epic points no longer crashes the game.


&+R06/01/26 - 06/30/26 - Groups, spells and fewer interruptions&n
&+W----------------------------------------------------------------------&n

&+CGroups and companions&n
- Pets join their owner's group automatically.
- Groups can be combined by grouping a willing group leader.
- Group recall no longer depends on grouping the cleric last.
- Group area spells no longer hit mounts ridden by you or your group.
- Paladin auras stay in place when a group leader is removed.
- Friendly guild golems on the same side count as grouped.

&+CSpells, skills and settings&n
- Mages can memorize the spells they have books for even if other books
  are missing.
- 'Improved invisibility' is now called 'invisibility'. The old name
  still works.
- Bards gain legend lore in the base class, and Scoundrels gain dual
  wield. Singing and group teleport correctly reveal a hidden singer.
- The innate list shows abilities you have not unlocked yet and the
  level needed to use them.
- Toggles can be set explicitly on or off instead of only being flipped.
- New-character equipment avoids weapons and items the character cannot
  use.
- Boon kill progress and Diamond Soul ending messages are clearer.

&+CItems, travel and reliability&n
- Fixed encrusting stripping weapon stats or accepting unsuitable items
  such as containers.
- Fixed bag weights and space checks, including bags inside other bags.
- Fixed the Deramuth ferry having both ends of its route in one room.
- Fixed guildhall construction and visibility mistakes on the who list.
- Improved recovery of pets, corpses, item descriptions and spell effects.
- Fixed several auction pickup, refund, locker exit and mail problems.
- Many crash and freeze fixes cover fighting, spells, pets, movement,
  quests, deaths and reconnecting. Saving is less likely to pause play.


&+R05/01/26 - 05/31/26 - Learning and clearer equipment&n
&+W----------------------------------------------------------------------&n
- Added a potion of learning, available from the shop in Mugnork in the
  Mountain of Peril Peaks. It gives chances for faster skill improvement
  for an hour.
- Epic skills stand out from regular skills in the 'skills' display.
- Ordinary zone equipment no longer receives random poor or superior
  quality changes.
- Language handling was simplified around speaking with your own side
  or the other side of the racewar.
- Tharnadia's rogue shop sells the vials needed for mixing poison.
- Fixed the Mugnork shop and cleaned up Peril Peaks descriptions.


&+R04/01/26 - 04/30/26 - Poisons, ferries and adventures&n
&+W----------------------------------------------------------------------&n

&+CAssassins, rogues and combat&n
- Assassins gain ambush and poison mixing at level 30. Use 'mixpoison'
  to prepare mixed poisons, then apply them to a suitable weapon.
- Apply poison can work with a wielded weapon and a vial on your belt,
  and can be used while waiting in ambush.
- Added poison effects that slow enemies, drain movement or cause
  madness. Fixed poison application and a crash when poison killed.
- Dirt toss has less delay. Blindness effects were made more reliable,
  with most lasting only a few combat rounds.
- Thieves gained higher limits for several fighting skills. Thieves and
  Assassins gained a higher disguise limit; Scoundrel trip was reduced.
- Anti-Paladins received stronger life-draining benefits, including
  Hellfire Absorb and Battle Ecstasy. Avernus's special attack improved.
- Fixed Monk critical hits so life-draining benefits, damage shields and
  the shorter combat display account for them properly.
- Race balance changed for Driders, Ogres, Firbolgs, Goblins, Githyanki,
  Tieflings and others. Check race help when choosing a new character.
- Githzerai can choose Paladin and Githyanki can choose Anti-Paladin.
  Driders wearing a spider body can be ridden.

&+CTravel, quests and rewards&n
- Expanded the ferry service to six ferries, with more stops and revised
  routes, speeds and waiting times. Bays were expanded at Myrabolus,
  Tharnadia and Sarmiz.
- Added wandering zone ambassadors to many areas. Their zone-completion
  reward increased from 250 to 1,000 platinum.
- Added scroll and ring quest content tied to the Mystic Ward and
  Winterhaven, plus a tradeskills teacher in Alatorin's miner guild.
- Fort Marigot gained a bartender. Grumbar and CRL2 gained epic stones.
- Improved rewards in Mount Banishment, Trakkia Mountains, Faerie Realm,
  Forgotten Mansion and other zones, with new rare treasures and enemies.
- Updated Arcium, Lava Springs, Fisherman's Wharf, Drifting Realm and
  Olyxs. Corrected Surface connections and several quest shops.
- IC3 was removed from the active world after its earlier balance pass.
- Identify and lore now show food effects. Alatorin food was updated.
- Fixed cargo displays, ferry shop purchases and Captain's flag rewards.

&+CRacewar and saving&n
- Revised racewar level-cap progression and the experience reward for
  the side that earns an increase. Later tuning is reflected in the
  game's current cap and reward displays.
- Frag lists show totals for both sides. Epic zones no longer change
  alignment as quickly.
- Fixed containers growing heavier incorrectly and improved saving of
  corpses, ships, character changes and account bank balances.


&+R02/01/26 - 02/28/26 - Connections and guild warnings&n
&+W----------------------------------------------------------------------&n
- Fixed disconnections when entering the game over a secure connection,
  and made slow connections less likely to fail during login.
- Fixed reconnecting to the wrong body and several website login,
  logout and auction problems.
- Guildhall magic mouths send their warnings to guild chat and handle
  same-side visitors correctly.
- Battle alerts start enabled by default.
- Added the Jestros chat channel and side choices for newbie assistance.


&+R01/01/26 - 01/31/26 - Shared storage and class updates&n
&+W----------------------------------------------------------------------&n

&+CAccounts, lockers and valuables&n
- Added account banks and account lockers, with racewar restrictions on
  locker use. Added private chests for protected storage.
- Fixed locker access grants for accounts and individual characters.
- Fixed equipment losing stats, gaining duplicate bonuses, changing
  type, or losing enhanced and encrusted effects after being stored.
- Fixed missing items inside stored bags and incorrect container weight.
- Inventory and bag contents keep their order when you log back in.
- Fixed items duplicating after resurrection or recovery from a crash.
- Improved recovery of pets and ships, including duplicate pets and
  ships appearing after a live restart.
- Fixed lost ship money and improved saving of experience, quest
  progress, guild membership and spellbooks.
- Picking up too many artifacts of the same class drops the extra
  artifact instead of making it disappear.

&+CHealers and holy magic&n
- Healers gained Warding Faith, a protective reserve that absorbs damage
  and recovers over time.
- Holymen gained Vital Intercession and Holy Intercession, which heal
  after damage is taken. The two protections can work together.
- Zealots gained Warring Zeal for accuracy and extra holy damage after
  melee hits, plus double attack at 41 and dual wield at 51.
- Zealot Flamestrike can leave a brand that reduces healing and
  life-draining recovery. Restore can remove it.
- Accelerated Healing was strengthened, and Group Heal casts faster.
- 'Tog heal' controls detailed healing messages. The shorter combat
  display combines more damage into a readable total.
- Prompts and target descriptions show ward protection.

&+CEthermancers, Dragoons and other combat&n
- Ethermancers gained Frost Beam. Ice Spikes and Lightning Ring were
  improved, while Blur was removed from their spell list.
- Tempest Magus Cyclone gained stronger level-based damage and the
  ability to stun elite monsters. Arcane Whirlwind scales with level.
- Anti-Magic Ray's dispelling and shrug behavior were adjusted.
  Disintegrate can bypass shrug some of the time; Acid Immolate does so.
- Evil Tieflings can be Ethermancers.
- Dragon Lancers gained shield block, and Dragoon spells received more
  fixes and balance work, including Edictum Cineris.
- Fixed two-handed extra attacks, thrown weapon damage and hit messages.
- Reduced equipment damage and corrected several damage calculations.
- Disguise kits no longer blind their users.

&+CPlaying and exploring&n
- Added in-game polls and a Hardcore leaderboard.
- Improved game-client displays for rooms, ships, combat and character
  changes. Hidden enemies and secret exits are better protected.
- Fixed several registration, login, inn rent and connection crashes.
- IC3 received a large monster and equipment balance pass during this
  period; it was later removed from the active world in April.


&+R12/14/25 - 12/31/25 - Guardians, Dragoons and healing&n
&+W----------------------------------------------------------------------&n

&+CGuardians and taunt&n
- Guardians can use two-handed weapons again.
- Dreadnaught's spell protection was strengthened, and crashes involving
  that protection and extra attacks were fixed.
- Taunt was added to more classes and specializations. It can target a
  different enemy while you are already fighting.
- Fixed monsters switching away from the person who successfully
  taunted them.

&+CDragoons and spell changes&n
- Added and refined Dragoon conjured weapons and spells, including
  Judicium, Sanguinis Ignis, Sanctum Draconis, Vivernae Concordia,
  Sigillum Negati and Draconic Apotheosis.
- Improved Dragoon communion timing, casting during combat, mount
  health and dragon breath. Corrected several spell and dodge messages.
- Healers became more focused on support: damage spells were removed,
  healing improved, and healing salve grew stronger with character level.
- Added Divine Font, which creates a short-lived source of healing,
  vitality and renewed movement that people can drink from.
- Group Heal moved to the tenth spell circle, and Accelerated Healing
  was improved. Further healing changes followed in January.
- Dispel magic can remove permanent protections from ordinary monsters
  and temporarily suppress them on elite monsters.
- Fixed spell protection using the attacker's resistance instead of the
  target's. Necromancer pets had excessive protection against players
  corrected, and Monk special hits received critical and life-drain fixes.

&+CArtifacts and world fixes&n
- The oaken staff gained Freedom of Movement with its intended waiting
  time. Axe of Dragonkind and other artifacts received improvements.
- Fixed Reflection disengaging its target and improved the dagger of
  Wind's chance to turn aside attacks.
- Corrected Sword of Fire and Flame and Mace of the Efreeti handling
  after the Brass area changes.
- Fixed an artifact timer that could make an artifact vanish far too
  soon. Dreamfoil now floats.
- Corrected zone resets that could restore equipment or clear a zone's
  epic completion before they should.

&+CAccounts and easier reading&n
- Switching racewar sides gained an account-wide waiting period, so
  changing characters does not skip the wait.
- Wizards gained spellbook summoning on login.
- Added support for playing through the website and richer displays in
  compatible game clients, including maps, groups and ship information.
- Fixed auction bids and item descriptions, duplicate sailing maps,
  paging prompts, account menu mistakes and several reconnect crashes.
- Tracking failure messages no longer reveal whether a hidden target
  exists just by giving a different error.


